  "version": "2026-11-02.2",
  "note": "Data only (selectors and regex strings). Modelled on typical retailer markup; NOT verified against the live sites. The owner must test and the server can ship a corrected version (scout?op=config). v1.7.3 store detection: `store` CSS selectors first, then `storeText` patterns (capture group 1 = store name) on the visible text of `storeAreas` (light DOM + open shadow roots), then on the top of the page. on=segments: one segment per element, joined with ' | '; on=text: all text, single spaces; on=label: aria-label/title. Delivery addresses are never read (lines with deliver… are skipped, names with digits are rejected). `online`: prices are national, store = Online. signedIn: `text` (strong, whole page), `re` (greeting, header only), `notText` (header shows a log-in link → not signed in). v1.7.3 selectors follow the owner's real page structure of 2 Nov 2026 (CSS-module hashes matched with [class*=…]); `storeMethod`: a store value only when the method is a pick-up one (never Delivery = home address); `tile.require`/`tile.skip`: real product tiles only; `signedIn.greet`: a greeting element; `storeIdJson`: the store id from the page's own JSON.",
